WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.820 --> 00:00:05.760
Star Wars: The Last Jedi delivers a soaring
blend of drama, action, and comedy—while

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:08.840
also tying up a few loose ends left in the
wake of The Force Awakens.

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:14.400
Writer-director Rian Johnson's chapter successfully
and perhaps controversially thrusts the franchise

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:18.970
forward in a number of meaningful ways, and
it does so largely by answering a few lingering

00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:20.280
questions along the way.

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:22.560
Warning: Major spoilers ahead.

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:24.140
Who are Rey's parents?

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:28.700
It seems that in the Star Wars universe, all
our favorite characters are related in some

00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:34.120
way: Darth Vader was Luke's father, Leia is
Luke's sister, Han Solo and Leia were married

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:39.160
for a time, and Kylo Ren — also known as
Ben Solo — is their angsty villainous son.

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:44.540
So when Rey was introduced in The Force Awakens,
questions regarding her true lineage ran rampant.

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:49.820
After years of speculating that Rey was somehow
related to Luke Skywalker or Obi-Wan Kenobi,

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:52.200
The Last Jedi put all the rumors to bed.

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:57.160
In one of the film's most subversive plot
twists, Rey faces a deep truth about her parents'

00:00:57.160 --> 00:01:01.320
identities: her parents were just a couple
of heartless nobodies who sold her off as

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:01.820
a child.

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:04.580
Of course this bombshell could just be a red
herring.

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:09.160
But in a series that has become notable for
secret familial ties, the notion that Rey

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:12.720
could be special just because she is makes
for a delightful change of pace.

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:14.840
Can Leia use Force powers?

00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:19.840
During the credits of The Last Jedi, "In loving
memory of our Princess, Carrie Fisher" appears

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:20.660
on the screen.

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:25.280
While that heartfelt goodbye acknowledges
Fisher's untimely passing, the Last Jedi's

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:28.260
story does not… but it does give her some
awesome powers.

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:31.540
Early on, Kylo Ren leads an attack on Leia's
ship.

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:34.520
There's a moment when Leia senses her son's
presence.

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:39.479
But while he successfully disposed of his
father in The Force Awakens, Kylo finds himself

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:40.880
unable to fire on his mother.

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:45.420
Instead, his minions do the dirty work and
Leia's body is thrown into space.

00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:50.420
But it turns out that Leia is as tapped into
the Force as her brother, and, as unbelievable

00:01:50.430 --> 00:01:55.049
as it seems, she uses the Force to navigate
through the crushing vacuum of space and back

00:01:55.049 --> 00:01:55.549
to safety.

00:01:55.680 --> 00:02:00.660
Back on her ship, Leia falls into a deep coma,
which she remains in for the majority of the

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:01.160
film.

00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:03.560
Why does Luke want the Jedi to end?

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:08.759
The ending of The Force Awakens found Rey
finally facing Luke Skywalker, the legendary

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:10.360
Jedi who'd gone into hiding.

00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:15.520
While fans were expecting an emotional meeting
between the two, things don't go down as planned.

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:19.900
When Rey finds him on the planet where the
first Jedi temple was built, Skywalker takes

00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:22.440
his old lightsaber and tosses it off a cliff.

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:24.780
Why is he so disdainful of the Jedi?

00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:29.340
It seems that Skywalker took the blame for
Kylo Ren's turn to the Dark Side.

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:34.060
This all stems from Luke's failure to train
Ben Solo in the ways of the Force.

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:38.400
When Solo was his student, Luke came close
to murdering him in his sleep, because he

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:41.680
was frightened by the deep well of darkness
he sensed in the boy.

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:46.640
Ben woke up to find Luke staring down at him
with lightsaber in hand, and responded with

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:47.600
a fiery rage.

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:52.380
Ben destroyed the Jedi school, many of its
students, and assumed he'd ended Skywalker

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:53.200
in the process.

00:02:53.590 --> 00:02:58.740
Following these events, Luke decides he wants
the Jedi to end because theirs was a legacy

00:02:58.750 --> 00:03:04.230
of hubris and failure—capped by Luke's own
epic failure, which turned Ben Solo into Kylo

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:06.800
Ren and helped fuel the rise of the First
Order.

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:09.320
Does Snoke's identity even matter?

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:14.560
When The Force Awakens hit theaters, speculation
ran rampant regarding Supreme Leader Snoke's

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:15.580
real identity.

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:20.980
Appearing only as a giant ominous hologram,
Snoke was presented as essentially the trilogy's

00:03:20.980 --> 00:03:21.600
new Emperor.

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:25.720
His motivations for turning Kylo Ren into
the next Darth Vader helped fuel the burning

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:27.440
question: who is this guy?

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:32.400
As frustrating as it may be, The Last Jedi
doesn't deliver any new revelations on that

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:32.900
front.

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:37.480
What the movie does do is finally give us
Snoke in the flesh as he dishes out pain to

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:43.070
Kylo, Hux, and even Rey … before a surprise
twist puts Kylo and Rey on the same team,

00:03:43.070 --> 00:03:44.760
destroying Snoke and his flashy guards.

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:50.840
When all's said and done, it seems Snoke's
true identity is … well, just Snoke.

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:55.760
While it's likely his backstory will be explored
elsewhere, as far as the sequel trilogy is

00:03:55.760 --> 00:04:00.180
concerned, it seems we've learned all we need
to know about Kylo Ren's former master.

00:04:01.180 --> 00:04:01.860
Thanks for watching!

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:04.740
